Unplanned executive departures are more common than succession plans assume. In our engagement data, one in four C-suite exits over the past three years happened with less than two weeks of notice.

## Stabilize Before You Search

Boards instinctively start a search. The better first move is stabilization: confirm decision rights, freeze non-critical initiatives, and appoint an interim executive with a defined mandate and end date.

## Communicate in Layers

Employees, lenders and key customers need different messages on different timelines. A single, sequenced communication plan protects confidence far better than a press release followed by silence.
